***************************** T A L Y S **************************7128 1451  143
                                                                  7128 1451  144
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   7128 1451  145
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      7128 1451  146
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    7128 1451  147
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     7128 1451  148
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  7128 1451  149
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        7128 1451  150
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    7128 1451  151
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         7128 1451  152
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      7128 1451  153
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    7128 1451  154
stored in this data file:                                         7128 1451  155
                                                                  7128 1451  156
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   7128 1451  157
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     7128 1451  158
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 7128 1451  159
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   7128 1451  160
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                7128 1451  161
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   7128 1451  162
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    7128 1451  163
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        7128 1451  164
- Recoil data                                                     7128 1451  165
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           7128 1451  166
- Total particle energy spectra                                   7128 1451  167
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      7128 1451  168
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        7128 1451  169
- Residual production cross sections                              7128 1451  170
                                                                  7128 1451  171
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            7128 1451  172
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        7128 1451  173
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   7128 1451  174
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                7128 1451  175
                                                                  7128 1451  176
